From: Antigravity <antigravity@google.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sched/cpufreq_schedutil: enforce up_rate_limit_us=0 and unhindered iowait boost

Set default up_rate_limit_us to 0 to eliminate frequency transition ramp-up delays
on CPU load spikes and ensure full immediate iowait_boost responsiveness on Xiaomi 14.

Signed-off-by: Antigravity <antigravity@google.com>
---
 kernel/sched/cpufreq_schedutil.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/kernel/sched/cpufreq_schedutil.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/cpufreq_schedutil.c
@@ -210,6 +210,8 @@ static void sugov_iowait_boost(struct sugov_cpu *sg_cpu, u64 time,
 		return;
 
 	/* Full iowait boost: scale instantly to max capacity */
+	sg_cpu->iowait_boost = sg_cpu->iowait_boost_max;
+	sg_cpu->iowait_boost_pending = true;
 }
@@ -750,7 +752,8 @@ static int sugov_init(struct cpufreq_policy *policy)
 	if (ret)
 		goto stop_kthread;
 
-	tunables->up_rate_limit_us = 500;
+	/* Enforce 0 latency up rate limit for maximum responsiveness */
+	tunables->up_rate_limit_us = 0;
 	tunables->down_rate_limit_us = 20000;
 
 	policy->governor_data = sg_policy;
-- 
2.43.0
